# Shared Libraries — Standards

> **Single source of truth. Changes here affect ALL apps.**

---

## 📦 Library Structure

| Library | Purpose | Used By |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-types` | Enums, interfaces, types | Backend + Frontend |
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-utils` | Backend decorators, helpers | Backend only |
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-ui` | Shared UI components | Frontend only |
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-theme` | Theme configuration | Frontend only |

---

## 🎯 Types Decision Tree

**Before creating ANY type, enum, or interface — ASK:**

```
Is this type needed by BOTH backend AND frontend?
│
├── YES → Put in `@oneohm-epc/shared-types`
│         Examples: CustomerStatus, ProjectPhase, PaginatedResponse
│
└── NO → Keep in the respective app
          │
          ├── Backend only → `apps/backend/src/modules/[feature]/types/`
          │   Examples: Internal service types, DB-specific types
          │
          └── Frontend only → `apps/web/lib/types/` or feature folder
              Examples: UI state types, form types, component props
```

---

## 📋 shared-types Guidelines

**PUT in shared-types:**
- ✅ Enums used in API responses (CustomerStatus, ProjectPhase, etc.)
- ✅ Interfaces for API request/response shapes
- ✅ Common types (PaginatedResponse, ApiError, etc.)
- ✅ Any type that appears in both apps

**KEEP in app:**
- ❌ Internal service types (backend only)
- ❌ UI component props (frontend only)
- ❌ Form validation schemas (frontend only)
- ❌ TypeORM-specific types (backend only)
- ❌ React Query key types (frontend only)

---

## 📝 Example: Where Types Go

```typescript
// ✅ shared-types — Used by both apps
export enum CustomerStatus {
  LEAD = 'lead',
  ACTIVE = 'active',
}

export interface PaginatedResponse<T> {
  data: T[];
  meta: { page: number; limit: number; total: number; totalPages: number };
}

// ❌ Backend only — Keep in apps/backend
interface CustomerRepositoryOptions {
  includeDeleted?: boolean;
  relations?: string[];
}

// ❌ Frontend only — Keep in apps/web
interface CustomerTableProps {
  customers: Customer[];
  onRowClick: (id: string) => void;
}
```

---

## ⚠️ Rules for Shared Libs

1. **Backward compatibility** — Never break existing APIs
2. **Minimal dependencies** — Keep libs lean
3. **Document changes** — Update README when adding features
4. **Test thoroughly** — Changes affect all apps

---

## 🚫 NEVER DO

❌ Put frontend-only types in shared-types  
❌ Put backend-only types in shared-types  
❌ Duplicate types across apps (consolidate to shared)  
❌ Import backend code in frontend or vice versa  
❌ Breaking changes without migration plan
